##NICHE SELECTION - THE PROBLEM FIRST FRAMEWORK 
The first step is to choose a niche for your ebook. Instead of selecting a topic simply based on personal interest, focus on identifying specific problems people are struggling with or goals they are willing to pay to achieve.



Identify Problems and Desires - 
Start by exploring different areas and identifying problems people want to solve.

Some examples include:
Finance: Budgeting, saving money and managing personal finances.
Career: Finding internships, resume building and interview preparation.
Business: Starting a side hustle, freelancing and finding clients.
Productivity: Time management, overcoming procrastination and building habits.
Fitness: Weight loss, muscle building and workout planning.
Education: Exam preparation, study techniques and learning new skills.

Focus on problems that can be addressed through a practical, actionable ebook.



Narrow Down Your Niche - 
Avoid choosing broad topics like Finance, Fitness or Business. Instead, narrow them down to a specific audience and problem.

For example:
Broad niche          Specific ebook idea
Finance              Personal budgeting for college students
Career               Internship hunting guide for freshers
Business             Starting a side hustle with no investment
Productivity         Time management for college students
Fitness              Home workouts for beginners

The winning formula:
1 Pain Point + 1 Clear Promise + 1 Actionable Solution.

For example:
Pain point: Students struggle to find internships.
Promise: Help students prepare an internship-ready profile.
Solution: A step-by-step guide covering resumes, LinkedIn, applications and outreach emails.



Validate Your Niche on Threads - 
Before creating your ebook, check whether people are actively discussing the problem on Threads.

How to do it:
Search for your selected topic directly on Threads.
Look for posts discussing the problems you want to solve.
Check their likes, replies and reposts.
Read the comments to understand what people are struggling with.
Look for repeated questions and requests for advice.
Identify topics where people are actively looking for solutions.

You can also explore Reddit, Quora and other online communities to understand your potential customers.



Research Existing Ebooks and Competitors - 
Once you identify a potential niche, check whether similar ebooks or digital products are already being sold.

How to do it:
Search for similar ebooks on Gumroad and other digital product marketplaces.
Check their pricing, descriptions and content offerings.
Read customer reviews to understand what buyers like or dislike.
Identify gaps in existing products.
Think about how your ebook can offer a more practical, detailed or beginner-friendly solution.



Things to Keep in Mind - 
Don't choose a niche solely based on personal interest.
Focus on problems people are genuinely willing to solve.
Avoid topics that are too broad.
Look for consistent demand rather than temporary trends.
Evaluate whether the audience has the willingness to pay.
Choose a problem you can provide a genuine and actionable solution for.
Don't assume that likes and engagement automatically translate into sales.




